In `mode <> prevMode` branch, if current mode invalid? But fault would have been true and caught earlier. So mode 0/1/2. If current mode changed from previous valid to current 0 or 1 => mode <>2 and outputs flowSP manual, valve prev. If changed to 2 => hold both. This matches. `normalMode` false. Good.

But requirements: "模式切换当拍不执行正常 PI 积分，normalMode=FALSE。切到串级 mode=2 时，flowSP 与 valveCommand 均保持上一拍值；切到自动/手动 mode=1/0 时，flowSP 跟随 manualFlowSP，valveCommand 保持上一拍值。" Exactly. If mode changed from 0 to 2 directly, hold previous (manual) outputs. Good.

Need "连续两拍切换也必须逐拍识别。" Suppose mode 0 -> 2 -> 1 over two cycles. First transition 0->2: mode =2, hold prev manual outputs, normal false, prevMode=2. Second transition 2->1: mode<>prevMode, not first/no fault/reset; mode=1, flowSP manual, valve hold previous (which outputs from first transition = prev manual valve). normal false. Good.

